# Proposed by a fixer (2026-10-15), from the random walks' finds; the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: whoever presses ⌘W or ⌘M asked to be rid of a window, not to be taken elsewhere. macOS hands the keyboard to the app's next
# window and says so a few milliseconds BEFORE it reports the closing. If that window is out of view, the view stays, nothing
# moves, and a window in view gets the keyboard.
# Reference: T07 T32. Decided in collab/QUESTIONS.md (product owner, 2026-10-15, "after ⌘W and ⌘M").
#
# Someone writes in Terminal, framed on its own, with a note floating over it. Safari is docked beside it, out of view.
open Notes 500x400
open Terminal
open Safari
dock 102 left
dock 103 right
zoom 102
# Into the Dock and out again: the note has come into view meanwhile and stays over the framed window.
minimize 102
flush
restore 102
flush
expect fills 102
expect visible 101
expect hidden 103
# A link opens a second Safari window over all that. It is read and closed.
open Safari 600x400
expect visible 104
close 104
flush
expect fills 102
expect hidden 103
# The note was swept out of view when the view went to Safari's other window and came back.
expect visible 101
# The same with the yellow button.
open Safari 600x400
minimize 105
flush
expect fills 102
expect hidden 103
expect visible 101
close 105
float-all
close 101
close 102
close 103
#
# A group is in view: a browser over notes and mail. The browser's other window is docked beside the group, out of view.
open Safari
open Notes
open Mail
open Safari
dock 106 right
dock 107 beside 106 bottom
dock 108 beside 107 right
dock 109 right
zoom 106
out
focus 106
expect visible 107
expect visible 108
expect hidden 109
# What is left of the group is no group of its own any more. The view used to end on everything, with notes and mail too small to show.
close 106
flush
expect visible 107
expect visible 108
expect hidden 109
# ⌘` to the browser's window out of view: nothing goes, so the view follows, a moment later.
open Safari 600x400
expect visible 110
focus 109
expect hidden 109
wait 0.05
expect visible 109
expect focused 109
